  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Intro by Disco Stu**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Banter (one)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Banter (two)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Track Seven**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Track Eight**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Banter (three)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Track Ten**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive1999-06-12.km184** (recommended): source not stated; 13 songs; 88 min [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive1999-06-12.km184**: taped by Thom Cooper; transferred by Paul deLima; source: (stage lip) Neumann KM184 (ORTF) > Apogee AD-1000 > AES/EBU cable > HHb PDR-1000 [1]. Also: Recorded from the stage lip with Neumann KM184 microphones in ORTF configuration, into an Apogee AD-1000 and HHb PDR-1000 DAT recorder; Transfer chain went from DAT through Sony PCM-R500 to HHb CDR-850 CD-R, then EAC, Sound Forge (with clipped peak restoration), CD Wave, and FLAC; Paul deLima transferred the recording and uploaded it to the LMA [1]",
